export const HOWTO: Sec[] = [
  { h: '1. Start on Home', p: 'The Dashboard shows your day: next prayer, tasks, spending and habits. Use the bottom bar to move between Home, Stats, Insights and Settings.' },
  { h: '2. Plan your days', p: 'Planner holds your tasks and events. Add an event and choose when to be reminded.' },
  { h: '3. Islamic Hub', p: 'Prayer times, Quran, zikir, fasting log and more. Prayer times use official Malaysian (JAKIM) zones, so they are only accurate in Malaysia. Allow location once so the right zone is found. In the Quran tab, Quran Audio plays any juz or surah and can save them for offline listening. Hafazan Check checks your recitation by voice: Learn, Test or Find. Open the how-to card on each tab to see the steps.' },
  { h: '4. Money and vehicles', p: 'My Finance tracks spending, income and commitments, and Today\'s spending lists what you spent today. My Accounts keeps the names and balances you enter for your cash, banks, wallets and cards, and links your spending and the Commitments you choose to them. This stays on your phone and is synced with your account like your other finance entries. No bank login or card number is ever asked for or stored. My Record keeps mileage, service and fuel for your vehicles. Maintenance can be counted in My Finance if you choose.' },
  { h: '5. Habit and Health', p: 'Log steps, sleep, mood and water. Turn on Count steps automatically to take steps from Health Connect or your phone\'s step sensor. Your streaks and score show up in Stats and Insights. The Patterns tab shows what the app notices in your own records. It has Experiments (with your own target number, notes, a History and an optional daily reminder) and a Time Machine with a Body hologram: tap a day or a part of the body, compare two days, see a simple estimate ahead, or turn the body with 3D view. The Progress tab shows how you are doing week by week. In the Today tab, under Sleep Tracker, you can keep a Heart log by typing your own pulse and blood pressure. In Today you can add Medication with reminders (tap Edit to change one later, and missed doses are marked) and use Relax for breathing and meditation. A private Cycle card can be turned on in Settings, Cycle & Wellbeing. Relax, energy, medicine and cycle also show in Insights and Stats.' },
  { h: '6. Family Planner', p: 'Open it from the Family Planner button in Daily Planner, or turn it on as a Dashboard module in Settings, Modules. The owner creates the family and shares the invite code from the Members page. Others join with the code, and children without a phone can be added as profiles. Together you share Tasks (chores and rewards), Household (shopping, menu and wishes) and Activities (a calendar with holidays and birthdays). Deleted things stay in Recently deleted for 7 days.' },
  { h: '7. Ask the Assistant', p: 'Type things like "I spent RM10 on lunch". It answers from your own data and can save entries for you. Try "remind me tomorrow 12pm to charge laptop" or "add milk to my shopping list". For anything else, tap Language and AI, then AI, to turn on Online AI or download Smart chat, which works with no internet.' },
  { h: '8. Keep it safe', p: 'Turn on App lock in Settings, Security. Save a backup now and then from Settings, Export. Hide modules you do not use in Settings, Modules. Export lets you choose whether turned-off modules go in the file.' },
];
export const FAQ: Sec[] = [
  { h: 'Which AI should I choose?', p: 'Online AI is the smartest and needs internet and sign-in. For no internet, pick Smart chat (small, fast), Smart chat+ (better) or, on phones with 12 GB of memory or more, Max. Max has Gemma 4 and Qwen 3.5. Qwen 3.5 is recommended. You can keep Online AI on as well. If it is not available, the AI on your phone helps.' },
  { h: 'Is my question private?', p: 'Smart chat runs on your phone and nothing leaves it. Online AI sends your question through our server to an AI service. We do not save it, but the service may handle it under its own policy, so do not type secrets.' },
  { h: 'The AI is slow the first time.', p: 'The model has to load into memory. It warms up when you open the Assistant, so the first answer should come sooner. Max models are slower and need a phone with enough free memory. Answers appear word by word while the AI writes.' },
  { h: 'Online AI says my daily limit is reached.', p: 'Each account has a small daily limit, and there is also a limit for everyone together. Try again tomorrow, or use Smart chat on your phone.' },
  { h: 'How do I activate the app?', p: 'Create an account, then enter the activation code you receive from the developer after payment. Each code works once and unlocks your account on all your devices.' },
  { h: 'Where is my data?', p: 'On your phone, encrypted, and backed up to your account online when you are signed in. Each account can only read its own data, apart from the Family Planner space you share with your family. The online copy is not end-to-end encrypted, so the developer could technically access it, but does not read it.' },
  { h: 'Can I use it on a new phone?', p: 'Yes. Install My Life 1.0, sign in with the same email and password, and your data comes back. Documents and Personal Collection details come back too. Receipt photos and the photos in Documents and Personal Collection are not included, because they stay on your phone. Move them with a backup file.' },
  { h: 'I changed phone. How do I move my data?', p: 'On the old phone, go to Settings, Export, choose Backup (JSON) and keep the file. On the new phone, open Settings, Security, Backup and restore, then Restore from a file. Photos from My Record receipts, Documents and Personal Collection come along in the backup file (up to 40 photos), and so do the documents and collection items themselves.' },
  { h: 'Steps do not count by themselves.', p: 'In Habit, turn on Count steps automatically and allow Physical activity. My Life 1.0 uses Health Connect when it has steps and your phone\'s own step sensor otherwise, and shows the larger number so nothing is counted twice. Open My Life 1.0 now and then to refresh the total. You can always add or correct steps by hand.' },
  { h: 'What does Budget left on Life Score mean?', p: 'It compares today\'s spending with the daily amount shown in My Finance. 100% means the whole daily amount is still free. 0% means it is used up or you are over. It only appears on days you have spent something.' },
  { h: 'How do I add my family?', p: 'Turn on Family Planner from Daily Planner or in Settings, Modules. The owner creates the family and shares the invite code from the Members page. Each person who joins needs their own account. Children without a phone can be added as profiles.' },
  { h: 'What happens to the family if I delete my account?', p: 'If you are a member, you leave the family and what you added stays for the others. If you are the owner, the family and everything in it are deleted. Hand over ownership first from the Members page if you want to keep it.' },
  { h: 'I forgot my PIN.', p: 'On the lock screen tap Forgot PIN. You can use your fingerprint or your account password to set a new PIN, or erase the app data and start fresh.' },
  { h: 'How do I set a medicine reminder?', p: 'Open Habit and Health, then the Today tab, and tap the Medication card. Tap + to add the medicine, its dose, the time and the days it repeats. You get a reminder at that time and again an hour later if you have not ticked it. My Life 1.0 does not give dose advice.' },
  { h: 'Can I change a medicine after saving it?', p: 'Yes. Open Medicine, tap the All medicines tab and tap Edit beside it. Change the name, dose, time, repeat or icon and tap Save changes. The reminder is rescheduled for you. If you change the time or days, older doses are not counted as missed.' },
  { h: 'What does Missed mean on a medicine?', p: 'A dose is Overdue for the first hour after its time and Missed after that if it is not ticked. Ticking a dose late still counts as taken. It is a personal record only, not medical advice.' },
  { h: 'How do I set a reminder?', p: 'Tap the search button on the Dashboard and choose Remind me, or open a note in Daily Planner, Notes & Reminders and tap the bell. Pick a time, and tap the buttons under Also alert me before if you want extra alerts. You can also tell the Assistant, for example "remind me tonight 9pm to charge phone".' },
  { h: 'Quran Audio does not play.', p: 'It streams over the internet by default, so check your connection and tap the surah or juz again, or tap the download arrow to save it and listen offline (Quran Audio, Downloads). If a reciter shows Not available, pick another one. To keep it playing with the screen off, allow notifications for My Life 1.0 and turn off battery saving for the app.' },
  { h: 'Can I listen to the Quran offline?', p: 'Yes. In Quran Audio tap the download arrow beside a surah or juz. Choose Wi-Fi only (recommended) or Wi-Fi and mobile data for downloads. The Downloads tab shows what is saved and its size, and lets you delete it. Tap Continue to pick up where you stopped.' },
  { h: 'Does Hafazan Check upload my voice?', p: 'No. It listens only while you recite, turns your voice into text on your phone and keeps no recording. The Quran model downloads once (about 57 MB) and you can remove it in Hafazan Check.' },
  { h: 'What do the colours mean in Hafazan Check?', p: 'Green means the word was heard. Yellow means the app is not sure about the word. Red means the word was not heard. The score shows how much you recited. Tap a yellow or red word to see what the model heard, and tap I said it right if you said it correctly. Recite a little slower, pause for about a second between verses, and try in a quiet place. It checks words only, not tajwid or madd, so confirm those with your teacher.' },
  { h: 'Why is vehicle maintenance in My Finance?', p: 'When you add maintenance spending in My Record, Today\'s spending asks once whether to count it in My Finance. If you say yes, it shows as a Vehicle category you can only change in My Record. You can switch it on or off any time from the note on Today\'s spending.' },
  { h: 'I turned a module off. Is my data gone?', p: 'No. It stays saved on your phone and in your online copy. The module just disappears from the Dashboard, Search, Stats, Insights, the Assistant and its reminders. In Export, a turned-off module starts unticked, so tick it if you want its data in the file. Turn the module back on in Settings, Modules.' },
  { h: 'Is a reminder an alarm?', p: 'Reminders ring like a normal notification, not like an alarm clock. They stay quiet if your phone is on silent or Do Not Disturb. Turn the phone sound on and allow notifications for My Life 1.0 to hear them. Medicine reminders are timed like an alarm clock so they are not held back (you can turn this off in Medicine, Never late).' },
  { h: 'Notifications do not ring.', p: 'Use Settings, General, Send a test notification. If nothing shows, allow notifications for My Life 1.0 in your phone settings and turn off battery saving for the app. If they arrive a few minutes late, tap Turn on exact timing in the same place and allow Alarms & reminders.' },
  { h: 'Prayer times look wrong.', p: 'Open Islamic Hub and refresh your location. Times follow JAKIM and are only accurate in Malaysia. Please confirm with your local authority.' },
];

